.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-DSP 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-dsp \- set direct-mixer, master, effect or routing controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-dsp\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] mixer SOURCE BUS CHANNEL PARAMETER VALUE [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-dsp\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] master SOURCE BUS CHANNEL PARAMETER VALUE [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-dsp\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] reverb PARAMETER BANK VALUE [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-dsp\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] route PAIR SELECTION [CTRL-PORT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a typed DSP control and print fresh state as JSON.
SOURCE is input or playback; BUS is A, B, C or D.
Mixer channels use 1..10; master channels use 1/2 (left/right).
Mixer link/mono use odd channels; master switches use channel 1.
.PP
Mixer parameters: link, mono, solo, mute, pan, volume, send.
Master parameters: link, volume, return, io-link.
Send and return belong to Mixer A's input section.
Reverb parameters: type (bank 0), pre-delay or time (banks 1..4).
Routing pairs use 1..5 and selections 0..8.
.PP
Arguments use decimal wire indices or coefficients rather than displayed units.
Run as the regular user with access to the ALSA device.
.PP
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR prints frame_hex JSON and opens no hardware.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
